 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "32: both tafsirs read «نور الله» as His religion; wind for «يطفئوا… بأفواههم», light for «يتم نوره». The reciter joins 32 to 33 (no clean cut), so 32-35 is one unit. 33: light for «بالهدى» (after «رسوله»), geometric for «على الدين كله»; As-Sa'di's «والسيف والسنان» is not used. 34 keeps «كثيرا» (many, not all) and Al-Muyassar's definition of hoarding (withholding zakat). Coins leave before «فبشرهم بعذاب أليم»; no gold motif and nothing drawn in 35 (Hell): night sky only. STAGING v4: c1 (32) stays ambient (their wish and Allah's refusal; both tafsirs: His light is His religion): the mood moves from light rays to night_sky so the light of Allah is not drawn as rays, and the light plate on the completing of His light becomes a lamp plate (the light of faith), after the Name. c2 (33) stays ambient (the sending of the Messenger); one light plate for guidance and the religion of truth, the geometric plate dropped (kept for the Names). c3 (34): a market by day; three believers stand at the left (the addressed, warned; As-Sa'di: a warning to the believers). The camera closes on them only on 34:3 (the address); while the scholars' deeds are recited (34:5-16) it stays wide and drifts to the market stalls (the people's wealth), never closing on the believers. The scholars and monks are not drawn (no people named; many, not all; nothing acted of the bribes): a coins plate for the people's wealth (34:10) and a two-paths plate for hindering from the way of Allah (34:13, gone before the Name). On 34:17 the believers leave the stage (long before the threat, so they are not in frame while it is recited) and a rich man walks in from the right (those who hoard; Al-Muyassar: withholding zakat), under a coins plate for the gold and silver (34:18, gone before 34:21); nothing is acted on the negation 34:21-25, and the camera holds on him, not on the believers, through 34:26-28; the address 34:26 gets camera only. c4 (35, Hell) stays ambient with no motif: no gold or fire drawn. The background stays quiet on 32:4-12 (His light) and 33:1-11 (He sent His Messenger)."
 },
